# Whitelist: Claude Code WRITES state into its config root (TESTED — a doctor run under a
# redirected CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR created .claude.json and backups/ inside it, docs/SHIP.md
# §2), and after the one-time login this directory holds the harness's credential state.
# Unlike the opencode config dir, which stays read-only, this one is mixed code+state, so
# everything is ignored except the tracked harness files named below. Fail-closed: a new
# state shape Claude Code invents lands ignored, not committed.
#
# CLAUDE.md is deliberately ABSENT from the whitelist: gate.py's banned-filenames check
# refuses that name anywhere in the tracked tree, so the tracked file is
# crew-constraints.md and env.claude.sh materializes the CLAUDE.md symlink at source time.
# No blanket agents/ or skills/ negations: user skills live UNDER this root, so a session
# could write there — a wholesale un-ignore would make that state stageable, which is the
# exact hole the whitelist exists to close (review finding). Add per-file negations when
# tracked agents/skills actually exist.
*
!.gitignore
!settings.json
!crew-constraints.md
!hooks/
!hooks/**
